+## v1.2.43.2.4 - Retain patch history in clean export
+
+- Keep the project `patches/` tree in `make export` so distributed/recovery patches remain available in the exported project context while generated `wharness-input-*`, `wharness-bundle-*`, `kernl-context-*`, `.orig` and `.rej` payloads remain excluded even when nested below `patches/`.
+- Update `EXPORT_INDEX.md` policy text and the export console summary to report how many patch/distribution files were retained.
+- Strengthen `export-check` so every source `patches/*.patch` file must be present in the archive instead of treating the whole patch tree as forbidden.
+- Preserve all v1.2.43.2.x clean-export protections, size/entry/SHA-256 reporting, ChatGPT embedded-auth fixes and deterministic frontend regression coverage.
+
 ## v1.2.43.2.3 - Clean export patches exclusion hotfix
 
 - Fix the clean exporter so the documented `patches/` exclusion is actually passed to `zip`; previous v1.2.43.2.x exports could still include the historical patch archive even though `EXPORT_INDEX.md` claimed it was omitted.
