@@ -1,3 +1,11 @@
+## v1.2.43.2.4 retained patch-history export regression
+
+- Operator requirement changed after v1.2.43.2.3: `patches/` is useful project/recovery context and must remain in the exported Wharness ZIP.
+- `scripts/export.sh` no longer excludes the `patches/` tree or rejects it in the fail-closed scan. Generated transport payload patterns remain globally excluded, including generated subtrees nested below `patches/`.
+- `make export` now reports a retained patch/distribution file count alongside path, size, entries and SHA-256.
+- `make export-check` compares the source `patches/*.patch` count with the archive count and fails if any patch is silently omitted; runtime/generated exclusions remain enforced.
+- Required regressions: a representative `patches/retain-me.patch` must survive export; a representative `patches/wharness-input-*/...` payload must not survive; `make export-check` must pass.
+
 ## v1.2.43.2.3 clean export patches exclusion regression
 
 - Reproduced from the operator run after v1.2.43.2.2: application/frontend/Desktop gates pass, `make export` produces an archive, then `export-check` rejects it because `patches/` is still present.
